<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aden is a port city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, built in the crater of an extinct volcano near the entrance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>. For centuries a hub of trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> under Yemeni dynasties such as the Zurayids and Rasulids, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1839 and became a major coaling station and colony. It was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> from 1967 to 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aden.jpg" alt="Aden" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahmedxalkatheri · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MallaDistrict.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
